if($path==='/methods/'){page_start('Evidence and methods','How the Beyond Spacetime companion distinguishes hypotheses, mathematical controls, verified computations and observational validation.',$path);?><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">SCIENTIFIC INTEGRITY</span><h1>Evidence before conclusions.</h1><p class="lead">An explanation is useful only if it makes clear what has been assumed, what has been calculated and what has actually been measured.</p></section><div class="grid two"><?php foreach([['01','Premise','A stipulated research proposition. It is not a measurement.'],['02','Conditional result','A consequence of a declared equation and initial state.'],['03','Numerical verification','A comparison against an independent formula, numerical reference or invariant.'],['04','Empirical validation','Independent observations distinguish a mechanism from competing explanations.']] as $v):?><article class="tile"><span class="eyebrow"><?=$v[0]?></span><h2><?=h($v[1])?></h2><p><?=h($v[2])?></p></article><?php endforeach;?></div><article class="prose section"><h2>Our comparison policy</h2><p>Use the conventional hot Big Bang and relativistic references where applicable; include zero-coupling, zero-gap and no-domain controls. Keep failures visible. Report the assumed parameters, units, limitations and complete numerical output. These learning experiments do not fit observational data.</p><p>See <a href="/concepts/evidence/">the evidence concept guide</a> for more detail, or consult the <a href="<?=ARC?>research-library/reproducibility/">ArcSecs reproducibility center ↗</a>.</p><h2>Discovery and machine-readable interpretation</h2><p>Each concept is server-rendered, independently addressable, and linked to related experiments and primary project sources. JSON-LD matches visible content. The catalog and local agent endpoint expose the same information without requiring a browser framework. Inclusion in search or AI systems is not guaranteed.</p></article><?php page_end();exit;}
if($path==='/agents/'){page_start('Agent interface','A native AG-UI 1.0 event subset and JSON experiment API for deterministic, source-linked learning workflows.',$path);?><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">HUMAN + MACHINE INTELLIGENCE</span><h1>Agent-ready from the start.</h1><p class="lead">Discover concept guides, run a bounded experiment and receive the same structured evidence the human interface displays. No API key, external AI provider or runtime SDK is required.</p></section><div class="grid two"><section class="panel"><h2>Local guide demonstration</h2><p>This is a deterministic guide, not a conversational language model. Choose a concept or an experiment and receive a real AG-UI event sequence.</p><form id="agent-form"><label for="agent-choice">Choose a guide or calculation</label><select id="agent-choice"><?php foreach(topics() as $t):?><option value="topic:<?=h($t['slug'])?>"><?=h($t['title'])?></option><?php endforeach;foreach(labs() as $l):?><option value="experiment:<?=h($l['id'])?>">Experiment: <?=h($l['title'])?></option><?php endforeach;?></select><button class="button" type="submit">Run local guide</button><button type="button" class="button secondary" id="agent-cancel" disabled>Cancel display</button></form><p id="agent-status" role="status">Choose an item to start.</p><div id="agent-answer" class="answer" aria-live="polite"></div><details><summary>Raw event stream</summary><pre id="agent-events" tabindex="0"></pre></details><noscript><p>The event demonstration requires JavaScript. The JSON catalog and documented API remain available.</p></noscript></section><section class="panel"><h2>Machine endpoints</h2><p><a href="/api/v1/catalog/">GET /api/v1/catalog/</a> — guides and parameter bounds.</p><p><code>POST /api/v1/experiment/</code> — JSON result, rows and metrics.</p><p><code>POST /api/ag-ui/</code> — server-sent AG-UI events.</p><p><a href="/.well-known/ag-ui.json">Capability discovery</a> (project-specific, not an official registry).</p><p>Supported events: RUN_STARTED, TEXT_MESSAGE_START, TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT, TEXT_MESSAGE_END, STATE_SNAPSHOT and RUN_FINISHED. State identifies a known topic or experiment. Requests are bounded to 32 KB; no external calls, tools, resume or persistent memory.</p></section></div><section class="prose section"><h2>Example agent request</h2><pre tabindex="0"><?=h(json_encode(['threadId'=>'demo','runId'=>'run-1','protocolVersion'=>'1.0','messages'=>[['id'=>'user-1','role'=>'user','content'=>'Run the bubble force control.']],'state'=>['experiment'=>'bubble','parameters'=>['pressure'=>1,'tension'=>.8,'radius'=>1.6]],'tools'=>[],'context'=>[]],JSON_PRETTY_PRINT|JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES))?></pre><p>POST this JSON with Content-Type: application/json to /api/ag-ui/. The endpoint validates the chosen parameters and emits a bounded SSE sequence. Invalid requests return HTTP 400 with a JSON error before the run starts.</p><h2>Compare two parameter sets</h2><p>Use <code>POST /api/v1/compare/</code> with an experiment identifier and objects named <code>left</code> and <code>right</code>. The response contains both complete numerical results and metric differences. <a href="/compare/">Open the human-facing comparison</a>.</p><h2>Protocol scope</h2><p>Implements a deliberately limited native subset of <a href="https://docs.ag-ui.com/spec/1.0/schema">AG-UI 1.0 ↗</a>. This is not a claim of full SDK interoperability or certification. The frontend uses native Fetch streams and JSON; it is also an example client.</p></section><?php page_end();exit;}
if($path==='/about/'){page_start('About this project','The role, sources and privacy practices of the Beyond Spacetime learning companion.',$path);?><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">THE PROJECT</span><h1>One research network. Two distinct experiences.</h1><p class="lead">BeyondSpacetime.org is the explanatory learning companion to ArcSecs.com, which remains the authoritative home for BEYOND SPACETIME, Scientific Review 6.0 and the full research archive.</p></section><article class="prose"><h2>Credit and scope</h2><p>The book credits Machine Intelligence and Michael Joseph Kappel and acknowledges Gary Lyon Otto for variable-speed-of-light ideas. This companion uses original explanatory text and small computational controls inspired by that research. For definitive wording, source data and licensing scope, consult <a href="<?=ARC?>publications/">ArcSecs publications ↗</a> and the <a href="https://github.com/MichaelKappel/ArcSecs.com/blob/main/LICENSE.md">original licensing notice ↗</a>.</p><h2>Privacy and dependencies</h2><p>The supplied site contains no analytics, tracking pixels, cookies, external fonts, advertising SDKs, remote scripts, accounts or databases. Lab and guide requests are computed locally on the PHP server and are not intentionally persisted by the application. Learning stage completion is saved only in your browser’s local storage if permitted; the itinerary has a reset control. Hosting providers may retain request and security logs; external destinations have their own privacy practices. No private .uai files or book archives are bundled.</p><h2>Scientific responsibility</h2><p>All alternative physical mechanisms are conditional or exploratory unless established by independent observations. The conventional references remain available; the site is not a substitute for scientific review.</p></article><?php page_end();exit;}
